<title>UK: Tea Plantations shares make quiet debut.</title>
<headline>Tea Plantations shares make quiet debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Tea Plantations Investment Trust Plc made a quiet debut on London Stock Exchange on Monday.</p>
<p>By 1200 GMT the shares were quoted at 99-1/2p, slightly below their 100p issue price. No trade was registered in the stock.</p>
<p>The investment trust, which is managed by Regent Fund Management (UK) Ltd and was valued at 6.26 million stg at the issue price, said it will invest in regional tea plantation companies in Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 1717 542 7945</p>
